<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (The reserveCap variable is the central integrity mechanism of the SGLD system. It represents the maximum SGLD mintable at any given time, and is updated exclusively by a dedicated reserve management role, itself gated behind a multi-signature approval process and a timelock delay on changes.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (reserveCap is increased only in direct correspondence with newly verified physical gold entering custody, never in anticipation of future acquisition. Syncrate maintains a deliberate operating buffer, holding somewhat more physical gold in custody than SGLD currently in circulation, replenished proactively as headroom narrows, rather than reactively in response to mint demand. This buffer exists specifically to avoid a scenario in which legitimate mint demand cannot be served promptly due to a temporary gap between fundraising and physical acquisition.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
